Fillets: a walk ends where one of its contacts reached the point where
the analytic piece after its guide starts (mitcad#1341).

Across a slight kink of the spine the walked guide's sections lean against
the analytic piece's: along a fin's top, coming to an arc's torus, the
contact on the chamfer reached the chamfer's cone where the torus starts
2.2 micrometres along the spine before the guide's end, the contact on the
top 4 micrometres short of the top's crease. The walk stopped there, its
contact across onto the cone, and the next step walked the 2.2 micrometres
to the guide's end: a piece whose faces the result's build could not join
to the torus, the arc's edge left on one face. The walk now ends where one
of its contacts lies within ten times the spine's tolerance of the point
on that side where the analytic piece after the guide starts (going back:
where the piece before it ends), as where it reaches the guide's end within
that tolerance (ChFi3d_ReachedAnalyticPiece).

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_top_creases.cpp, the rounding of a
reported fin's top across creases of 1.4 and 2.2 degrees: built and closed,
the stored body after it on the result within 0.01 mm (with patch 1300
alone the result has an edge on one face only).

Upstream: new.

